**How to implement.** The section proved end to end through the kit window and a real folder, and the gotcha a later reader needs (001 §K; 001 §E notes in the files; the S9.1 brief; AGENTS.md: wait for deterministic conditions, drive by id). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests/KitWindowTests.fs` (steps 184, 284) gains the ui-smoke fact `a two-variable experiment recorded through the bay keeps its scan, role, session and notes in its kit file`: over a folder kit under the class's test directory opened read-write through `openKitAt` and mounted through `kitWindowView` as step 284's fact mounts it, with a sample bound to the 1 mm glass plate added between the seeded source and detector and the Experiments bay open: pressing the sample's candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r2`, `experimentAddScanAxisButton`, the candidate, `ExperimentVariable_r1` and `experimentAddButton`, then `experimentRoleChoice` of `calibration`, and typing `Day 1` into `experimentSessionField` and `LR re-seated` into `experimentNotesField`, each committed by Enter, leaves the folder holding `E1.experiment-json` (the standard template cannot name a table with no item in Prep 1) whose experiment, read back through `readExperiments` of the folder reopened through `openKitAt`, has one block of the two axes, `CalibrationRun`, `Some (SessionName "Day 1")` and the notes `LR re-seated`, and the row `ExperimentBadge_1` reads `no data`. (2) `AGENTS.md`, after the gotcha 'Names come from the kit's naming template' (step 276), one bullet of at most six lines: **An experiment is a scan over a setup revision** (`Experiments.fs`, spec 0050 S9.1): blocks of axes, each axis one variable of one slot over its range (a dial-mounted item scans its raw reading); a block is the product of its axes, the first outermost, read on its capture; its name comes from the kit's template (else `E<n>`) and is its file's stem; its role, session and notes and its mapped attachment (import profile and row selection) live in its file; its data badge is `ExperimentDataBadge.ofCheck`. Nothing else in the file changes.

**Acceptance.** After the acceptance lands, a two-variable experiment recorded through the kit window's bay MUST be read back from its folder with its scan, role, session and notes, and AGENTS.md MUST carry the gotcha 'An experiment is a scan over a setup revision'; ui-smoke MUST pass, including `a two-variable experiment recorded through the bay keeps its scan, role, session and notes in its kit file`, the count rising by 1; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, their count unchanged; and build, elevation and the sixteen s29 invariants MUST pass.
